    "text": "One plano-convex&nbsp;and one plano-concave lens of the same radius of curvature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;but of different materials are joined side by side as shown in the figure. If the refractive index of the material of <math><mn>1</mn></math> is <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and that of <math><mn>2</mn></math> is<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>, then the focal length of the combination is:<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/jee_physoc.JPG\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 60px; height: 67px;\" />",
